{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Gestión de columnas de `scada_proc`\n",
    "\n",
    "Notebook utilitario para **reorganizar, añadir y borrar columnas** de la tabla `scada_proc` (Delta en Lakehouse) de forma sistemática y segura.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Cosas que hace**:\n",
    "1. Inspecciona el esquema actual y muestra las columnas agrupadas por familia.\n",
    "2. Aplica un **orden canónico** (identificadores → sensores crudos → derivados → flags → metadata).\n",
    "3. Funciones reutilizables: `add_column`, `drop_column`, `reorder_columns`, con flag `dry_run`.\n",
    "4. Backup previo a operaciones destructivas (tabla `scada_proc_backup_<ts>`).\n",
    "5. Validación: cuenta de filas antes/después, lista de columnas perdidas.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Ejecución recomendada**: célula por célula, con `dry_run=True` la primera vez."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Parámetros\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "TABLE       = 'scada_proc'\n",
    "DRY_RUN     = True     # True = no escribe nada, solo muestra. Cambiar a False para aplicar.\n",
    "DO_BACKUP   = True     # Antes de cualquier reescritura, hace copia 'scada_proc_backup_<ts>'.\n",
    "PARTITION   = 'plant_code'  # Columna de particionado actual."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "# Setup\n",
    "# ============================================================\n",
    "import re\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "from pyspark.sql import functions as F\n",
    "\n",
    "def _ts():\n",
    "    return datetime.now().strftime('%Y%m%d_%H%M%S')\n",
    "\n",
    "def _table_columns(table):\n",
    "    return spark.table(table).columns\n",
    "\n",
    "def _table_schema(table):\n",
    "    return {f.name: f.dataType.simpleString() for f in spark.table(table).schema.fields}\n",
    "\n",
    "def _row_count(table):\n",
    "    return spark.table(table).count()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Tabla: {TABLE}')\n",
    "print(f'Existe: {spark.catalog.tableExists(TABLE)}')\n",
    "print(f'DRY_RUN: {DRY_RUN}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Inspección del estado actual\n",
    "\n",
    "Lista las columnas agrupadas por familia para que veas el caos antes de reorganizar."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Familias de columnas: prefijo o patrón -> nombre del grupo\n",
    "FAMILY_RULES = [\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^(plant_code|Date)$', re.I),  '0_id'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^POA_', re.I),                '1_poa'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^GHI_', re.I),                '2_ghi'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^DHI_', re.I),                '3_dhi'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^REF_', re.I),                '4_ref'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^T_AMB', re.I),               '5_t_amb'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^T_MOD', re.I),               '6_t_mod'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^WIND', re.I),                '7_wind'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^ALB(_|$)', re.I),            '8_albedo'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^(P_|E_|POWER|ENERGY)', re.I),'9_pwr_energy'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'_filt$', re.I),               'A_filtered'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'_flag$', re.I),               'B_flags'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'^c\\d+$', re.I),               'C_criteria'),\n",
    "    (re.compile(r'(ingested_at|source_file|updated_at|loaded_at)$', re.I), 'Z_metadata'),\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "def family_of(col):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Devuelve la 'familia' de una columna según FAMILY_RULES. 'X_misc' si no encaja.\"\"\"\n",
    "    for rx, fam in FAMILY_RULES:\n",
    "        if rx.search(col):\n",
    "            return fam\n",
    "    return 'X_misc'\n",
    "\n",
    "def grupos_actuales(table):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Agrupa las columnas actuales de `table` por familia.\"\"\"\n",
    "    cols = _table_columns(table)\n",
    "    grupos = {}\n",
    "    for c in cols:\n",
    "        grupos.setdefault(family_of(c), []).append(c)\n",
    "    return grupos\n",
    "\n",
    "if spark.catalog.tableExists(TABLE):\n",
    "    grupos = grupos_actuales(TABLE)\n",
    "    print(f'Total columnas: {sum(len(v) for v in grupos.values())}')\n",
    "    print(f'Total filas:    {_row_count(TABLE):,}')\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    for fam in sorted(grupos.keys()):\n",
    "        print(f'  [{fam}]  {len(grupos[fam])} cols')\n",
    "        for c in grupos[fam]:\n",
    "            print(f'    - {c}')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('La tabla no existe.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Definición del orden canónico\n",
    "\n",
    "Las columnas se reordenan respetando este orden de familias:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. `0_id` — identificadores (plant_code, Date)\n",
    "2. `1_poa` … `4_ref` — irradiancia (sensores crudos)\n",
    "3. `5_t_amb`, `6_t_mod` — temperaturas\n",
    "4. `7_wind`, `8_albedo` — viento, albedo\n",
    "5. `9_pwr_energy` — potencia y energía\n",
    "6. `A_filtered` — derivados / filtrados\n",
    "7. `B_flags` — flags de calidad\n",
    "8. `C_criteria` — criterios c1..cN\n",
    "9. `X_misc` — el resto (ojo si aparece mucho aquí, revisa FAMILY_RULES)\n",
    "10. `Z_metadata` — ingested_at, source_file, etc.\n",
    "\n",
    "Dentro de cada familia, **alfabético**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def orden_canonico(cols):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Reordena `cols` según FAMILY_RULES + alfabético dentro de cada familia.\"\"\"\n",
    "    enriched = [(family_of(c), c) for c in cols]\n",
    "    enriched.sort(key=lambda t: (t[0], t[1].lower()))\n",
    "    return [c for _, c in enriched]\n",
    "\n",
    "if spark.catalog.tableExists(TABLE):\n",
    "    orig = _table_columns(TABLE)\n",
    "    nuevo = orden_canonico(orig)\n",
    "\n",
    "    print('--- Orden actual ---')\n",
    "    for c in orig:\n",
    "        print(f'  {c}')\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    print('--- Orden propuesto ---')\n",
    "    for c in nuevo:\n",
    "        print(f'  {c}')\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    cambian = sum(1 for a, b in zip(orig, nuevo) if a != b)\n",
    "    print(f'Columnas en distinta posición: {cambian} / {len(orig)}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Funciones reutilizables — añadir, borrar, reordenar\n",
    "\n",
    "Tres funciones que puedes usar en cualquier momento. Todas respetan `DRY_RUN` y hacen backup si `DO_BACKUP=True`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def _backup(table):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Snapshot de la tabla en `<table>_backup_<timestamp>`.\"\"\"\n",
    "    backup_name = f'{table}_backup_{_ts()}'\n",
    "    if DRY_RUN:\n",
    "        print(f'  [DRY] backup -> {backup_name}')\n",
    "        return backup_name\n",
    "    spark.sql(f'CREATE TABLE {backup_name} AS SELECT * FROM {table}')\n",
    "    n = _row_count(backup_name)\n",
    "    print(f'  backup creado: {backup_name} ({n:,} filas)')\n",
    "    return backup_name\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def add_column(table, col_name, dtype='DOUBLE', default=None):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Añade una columna nueva.\n",
    "    - dtype: tipo SQL ('DOUBLE', 'STRING', 'TIMESTAMP', 'INT'...).\n",
    "    - default: valor por defecto (None = NULL). Solo aplicable si DRY_RUN=False.\n",
    "    Operación rápida e idempotente (no falla si ya existe).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    existing = _table_columns(table)\n",
    "    if col_name in existing:\n",
    "        print(f'  [skip] {col_name} ya existe en {table}')\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    print(f'  add: {table}.{col_name} {dtype} default={default!r}')\n",
    "    if DRY_RUN:\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    spark.sql(f'ALTER TABLE {table} ADD COLUMNS (`{col_name}` {dtype})')\n",
    "    if default is not None:\n",
    "        spark.sql(f'UPDATE {table} SET `{col_name}` = {default!r} WHERE `{col_name}` IS NULL')\n",
    "    print(f'  OK')\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def drop_column(table, col_name):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Elimina una columna. Requiere que la tabla tenga columnMapping habilitado.\n",
    "    Si no lo tiene, lo activa primero (TBLPROPERTIES).\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    existing = _table_columns(table)\n",
    "    if col_name not in existing:\n",
    "        print(f'  [skip] {col_name} no existe en {table}')\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    if col_name in (PARTITION, 'Date', 'plant_code'):\n",
    "        raise ValueError(f'No se puede borrar {col_name}: es identificador/partición')\n",
    "    print(f'  drop: {table}.{col_name}')\n",
    "    if DRY_RUN:\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    if DO_BACKUP:\n",
    "        _backup(table)\n",
    "    # Habilitar columnMapping si no lo está (necesario para DROP COLUMN en Delta)\n",
    "    spark.sql(f\"\"\"ALTER TABLE {table} SET TBLPROPERTIES (\n",
    "        'delta.columnMapping.mode' = 'name',\n",
    "        'delta.minReaderVersion' = '2',\n",
    "        'delta.minWriterVersion' = '5'\n",
    "    )\"\"\")\n",
    "    spark.sql(f'ALTER TABLE {table} DROP COLUMN `{col_name}`')\n",
    "    print(f'  OK')\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def reorder_columns(table, new_order):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Reordena las columnas de la tabla según `new_order`. Reescribe la tabla\n",
    "    completa (operación cara pero segura).\n",
    "    Valida que las columnas coincidan exactamente: no se pueden añadir/quitar aquí.\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    actuales = _table_columns(table)\n",
    "    set_a, set_n = set(actuales), set(new_order)\n",
    "    if set_a != set_n:\n",
    "        sobran = set_n - set_a\n",
    "        faltan = set_a - set_n\n",
    "        raise ValueError(\n",
    "            f'new_order no coincide con tabla.\\n'\n",
    "            f'  sobran: {sobran}\\n'\n",
    "            f'  faltan: {faltan}'\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    if actuales == new_order:\n",
    "        print(f'  [skip] {table} ya está en el orden deseado')\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    print(f'  reorder: {table} ({len(actuales)} columnas)')\n",
    "    if DRY_RUN:\n",
    "        return\n",
    "    if DO_BACKUP:\n",
    "        _backup(table)\n",
    "    n_pre = _row_count(table)\n",
    "    df = spark.table(table).select(*new_order)\n",
    "    writer = df.write.format('delta').mode('overwrite').option('overwriteSchema', 'true')\n",
    "    if PARTITION in new_order:\n",
    "        writer = writer.partitionBy(PARTITION)\n",
    "    writer.saveAsTable(table)\n",
    "    n_post = _row_count(table)\n",
    "    if n_pre != n_post:\n",
    "        raise RuntimeError(f'PERDIDA DE DATOS: {n_pre:,} -> {n_post:,} filas')\n",
    "    print(f'  OK ({n_pre:,} filas conservadas)')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Ejemplos de uso\n",
    "\n",
    "Comenta/descomenta lo que necesites. Con `DRY_RUN=True` solo imprime el plan, sin tocar nada."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# --- Añadir una columna nueva ---\n",
    "# add_column(TABLE, 'POA_5', dtype='DOUBLE')\n",
    "# add_column(TABLE, 'comentario', dtype='STRING')\n",
    "# add_column(TABLE, 'es_anomalia', dtype='BOOLEAN', default=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Borrar una columna ---\n",
    "# drop_column(TABLE, 'GHI_5_filt_old')   # falla si no existe (lo dice por log, no aborta)\n",
    "# drop_column(TABLE, 'plant_code')        # IMPOSIBLE: es la partición\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- Reordenar al orden canónico ---\n",
    "# nuevo_orden = orden_canonico(_table_columns(TABLE))\n",
    "# reorder_columns(TABLE, nuevo_orden)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Reorganización completa (en producción)\n",
    "\n",
    "Ejecuta esto cuando hayas verificado el plan con `DRY_RUN=True`:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Cambia `DRY_RUN = False` en la primera celda de parámetros.\n",
    "2. Asegúrate de que `DO_BACKUP = True` para tener red de seguridad.\n",
    "3. Ejecuta la celda siguiente."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Reorganización completa\n",
    "if not spark.catalog.tableExists(TABLE):\n",
    "    print('Tabla no existe.')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    n_pre = _row_count(TABLE)\n",
    "    cols_pre = _table_columns(TABLE)\n",
    "    print(f'Estado pre-reorden:')\n",
    "    print(f'  filas: {n_pre:,}')\n",
    "    print(f'  cols:  {len(cols_pre)}')\n",
    "    print()\n",
    "    nuevo = orden_canonico(cols_pre)\n",
    "    reorder_columns(TABLE, nuevo)\n",
    "    if not DRY_RUN:\n",
    "        n_post = _row_count(TABLE)\n",
    "        cols_post = _table_columns(TABLE)\n",
    "        print()\n",
    "        print(f'Estado post-reorden:')\n",
    "        print(f'  filas: {n_post:,}   (diff: {n_post - n_pre:+d})')\n",
    "        print(f'  cols:  {len(cols_post)}')\n",
    "        assert n_pre == n_post, 'PERDIDA DE FILAS'\n",
    "        assert set(cols_pre) == set(cols_post), 'PERDIDA DE COLUMNAS'\n",
    "        print('  Validación OK')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Rollback\n",
    "\n",
    "Si algo va mal después de aplicar, puedes restaurar desde el backup:\n",
    "\n",
    "```python\n",
    "# Lista backups disponibles\n",
    "for t in spark.catalog.listTables():\n",
    "    if t.name.startswith('scada_proc_backup_'):\n",
    "        print(t.name)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Restaurar (con cuidado: sobreescribe scada_proc actual)\n",
    "BACKUP = 'scada_proc_backup_20260616_113000'  # ← rellenar con el real\n",
    "spark.sql(f'DROP TABLE IF EXISTS scada_proc')\n",
    "spark.sql(f'CREATE TABLE scada_proc AS SELECT * FROM {BACKUP}')\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "Alternativa con Delta time travel (si no borraste el backup y la tabla original sigue siendo Delta):\n",
    "\n",
    "```sql\n",
    "DESCRIBE HISTORY scada_proc;\n",
    "-- Identifica la versión previa a la reescritura, p. ej. v=12\n",
    "RESTORE TABLE scada_proc TO VERSION AS OF 12;\n",
    "```"
   ]
  }
